1
00:01:37,910 --> 00:01:43,930
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,060 --> 00:01:46,810
[Episode 18]

3
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:12,960
Well...

4
00:02:15,360 --> 00:02:16,680
I searched through
more than a dozen train cars

5
00:02:16,680 --> 00:02:17,740
before I found you.

6
00:02:19,430 --> 00:02:20,870
W-Why are you...

7
00:02:21,150 --> 00:02:22,480
It's not because of you.

8
00:02:25,710 --> 00:02:27,310
It's not only because of you.

9
00:02:35,829 --> 00:02:36,640
Zhengliang!

10
00:02:42,910 --> 00:02:44,370
Have a drink before you go.

11
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:47,460
I thought you'd already left.

12
00:02:48,079 --> 00:02:49,610
Why didn't you go to Guilin?

13
00:02:52,310 --> 00:02:53,520
I made all that up.

14
00:02:55,030 --> 00:02:55,810
I didn't hear back

15
00:02:55,810 --> 00:02:57,430
from a single hospital.

16
00:03:00,590 --> 00:03:01,910
I just don't get it.

17
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:03,910
How did Chen ever fall for you?

18
00:03:05,190 --> 00:03:06,450
You're not just broke.

19
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:08,470
You lie too.

20
00:03:09,430 --> 00:03:10,680
And on top of that,

21
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:12,630
you're sick.

22
00:03:13,430 --> 00:03:14,710
Mentally.

23
00:03:15,330 --> 00:03:17,390
Physically, I'm perfectly healthy.

24
00:03:18,630 --> 00:03:19,310
Yeah.

25
00:03:23,870 --> 00:03:24,520
Fine.

26
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:26,190
I'm sick.

27
00:03:31,370 --> 00:03:32,230
Can it kill you?

28
00:03:32,520 --> 00:03:33,310
What?

29
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:36,820
I asked if your condition could kill you.

30
00:03:36,940 --> 00:03:38,160
In theory, no.

31
00:03:39,630 --> 00:03:41,170
In theory, no.

32
00:03:41,310 --> 00:03:42,840
Then what are you afraid of?

33
00:03:45,430 --> 00:03:46,490
I'm afraid of pain.

34
00:03:48,710 --> 00:03:49,630
Afraid of pain?

35
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:52,560
All the more reason to go back with Chen.

36
00:03:53,079 --> 00:03:54,560
What heals pain

37
00:03:54,710 --> 00:03:55,520
better than

38
00:03:55,590 --> 00:03:56,910
family and friends?

39
00:03:58,760 --> 00:03:59,750
Well, you haven't told

40
00:03:59,750 --> 00:04:01,590
your mom you're sick either, have you?

41
00:04:01,590 --> 00:04:02,550
That's because I never

42
00:04:02,550 --> 00:04:05,190
got the chance to tell her,
and now it's too late.

43
00:04:05,190 --> 00:04:06,000
Look.

44
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:10,560
Chemotherapy

45
00:04:11,190 --> 00:04:12,080
can't save me.

46
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,560
Neither can tears.

47
00:04:14,630 --> 00:04:16,160
I'm going to die either way.

48
00:04:17,750 --> 00:04:19,040
I'll face it alone.

49
00:04:19,310 --> 00:04:21,110
You can't go through this alone.

50
00:04:21,310 --> 00:04:22,840
When that day really comes,

51
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:26,360
it'll only hurt your mom even more.

52
00:04:30,830 --> 00:04:31,630
Maybe.

53
00:04:33,870 --> 00:04:35,270
But I don't have a choice.

54
00:04:36,430 --> 00:04:37,390
Neither do I.

55
00:04:39,630 --> 00:04:40,730
Then let me share

56
00:04:40,750 --> 00:04:42,150
a theory of mine with you.

57
00:04:43,070 --> 00:04:43,960
Pain and memory

58
00:04:43,980 --> 00:04:45,270
cannot be separated.

59
00:04:45,510 --> 00:04:47,040
People can't simply

60
00:04:47,310 --> 00:04:49,270
choose to erase their memories.

61
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:51,390
Even if you pretend to want to forget,

62
00:04:51,390 --> 00:04:52,720
the pain is still there.

63
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:55,390
Simple example:

64
00:04:56,430 --> 00:04:58,290
this bottle of soy milk in my hand.

65
00:04:58,430 --> 00:04:59,560
If I put it down there

66
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:00,430
on the ground,

67
00:05:00,750 --> 00:05:01,740
it looks like

68
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:02,800
it's no longer in my hand.

69
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:04,530
But it's still there, isn't it?

70
00:05:04,830 --> 00:05:05,630
Get it?

71
00:05:10,510 --> 00:05:11,310
Look.

72
00:05:12,510 --> 00:05:14,310
This is also a bottle of soy milk.

73
00:05:20,270 --> 00:05:20,920
Look,

74
00:05:21,630 --> 00:05:23,270
if you drink it, it's gone.

75
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:25,190
Isn't it still in your stomach?

76
00:05:25,190 --> 00:05:26,510
Just wait for your body to digest it.

77
00:05:26,510 --> 00:05:28,120
Then it'll turn into urine,
and you pee it out.

78
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,490
It can't be digested.

79
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:32,270
It's a figure of speech.

80
00:05:32,510 --> 00:05:33,360
"Metaphor."

81
00:05:33,630 --> 00:05:34,390
Get it?

82
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,070
It's a metaphor.

83
00:05:36,159 --> 00:05:37,950
You can't put it into words.

84
00:05:38,070 --> 00:05:38,800
Just like...

85
00:06:03,650 --> 00:06:10,810
♪ It's only after something is lost
that we begin to see ♪

86
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,120
Okay, okay.

87
00:06:08,190 --> 00:06:09,000
You win.

88
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:10,920
It's gone.

89
00:06:12,750 --> 00:06:18,440
♪ But some things can never be undone ♪

90
00:06:17,630 --> 00:06:18,390
Zhengliang.

91
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:21,510
If you have nowhere to go,

92
00:06:21,460 --> 00:06:27,990
♪ When snowflakes cover
all our yesterdays ♪

93
00:06:22,510 --> 00:06:23,430
just go home.

94
00:06:25,630 --> 00:06:26,630
As long as you're alive,

95
00:06:26,630 --> 00:06:27,960
you still have choices.

96
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:30,240
At least you still have choices.

97
00:06:29,370 --> 00:06:35,260
♪ Perhaps it's best
we leave the words unsaid ♪

98
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:37,240
I'm sorry.

99
00:06:39,260 --> 00:06:46,480
♪ We were once someone else ♪

100
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:42,000
I'm just saying.

101
00:06:43,830 --> 00:06:45,890
Whether you go home or not is up to you.

102
00:06:46,070 --> 00:06:47,530
No need to apologize to me.

103
00:06:48,090 --> 00:06:54,140
♪ Then, one day,
we found our truest selves ♪

104
00:06:48,630 --> 00:06:49,890
I'm apologizing to you

105
00:06:51,270 --> 00:06:53,430
because I shouldn't have
compared us like that.

106
00:06:53,430 --> 00:06:55,159
Our situations are different.

107
00:06:56,980 --> 00:07:03,910
♪ Turns out,
you don't have to fall apart ♪

108
00:07:00,430 --> 00:07:01,240
Accepted.

109
00:07:04,630 --> 00:07:12,220
♪ To deserve a fresh start ♪

110
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:14,890
[Dream Garden]

111
00:07:14,870 --> 00:07:21,620
♪ Not every goodbye is meant to
erase the past ♪

112
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:30,550
♪ At least we met with open hearts ♪

113
00:07:32,159 --> 00:07:35,150
♪ When life stretches on for so long ♪

114
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:33,390
Zhengliang!

115
00:07:35,880 --> 00:07:39,670
♪ Not every story needs a perfect ending ♪

116
00:07:36,510 --> 00:07:37,310
Bye-bye!

117
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:48,390
♪ Maybe walking side by side
for a while is enough ♪

118
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:53,730
So you mean

119
00:07:54,510 --> 00:07:56,570
Pink Hair managed to talk you into it?

120
00:07:58,310 --> 00:07:59,260
The same words

121
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:00,390
just hit differently

122
00:08:00,390 --> 00:08:02,050
coming from you than from him.

123
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:05,620
Actually, deep down,

124
00:08:05,620 --> 00:08:07,070
I was still wavering

125
00:08:08,110 --> 00:08:09,750
until I saw someone.

126
00:08:24,510 --> 00:08:27,240
Son, Happy New Year.

127
00:08:32,870 --> 00:08:34,150
Son, look.

128
00:08:36,150 --> 00:08:37,409
Those migratory birds

129
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:40,480
fly south for the winter,

130
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,600
but when spring comes,

131
00:08:43,080 --> 00:08:44,210
they always return.

132
00:08:47,630 --> 00:08:49,550
They know where they want to go.

133
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:03,440
Happy New Year.

134
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:06,550
I think

135
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:09,150
that might mean I've taken

136
00:09:09,670 --> 00:09:11,270
a step forward emotionally.

137
00:09:11,870 --> 00:09:13,020
And after everything that's happened,

138
00:09:13,020 --> 00:09:14,960
I guess it was also the result of...

139
00:09:15,790 --> 00:09:17,600
of a combination of factors.

140
00:09:18,550 --> 00:09:20,880
I didn't understand a single word of that,

141
00:09:21,270 --> 00:09:22,320
but I like how you

142
00:09:22,340 --> 00:09:23,860
act all profound.

143
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:25,200
I'm not acting...

144
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:25,960
Okay.

145
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:27,960
Profound without even realizing it.

146
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:28,670
Happy now?

147
00:09:31,750 --> 00:09:34,360
Actually, my mom and your mom
were very close.

148
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:36,770
But I don't know much about her.

149
00:09:36,770 --> 00:09:38,300
What kind of person was she?

150
00:09:44,390 --> 00:09:45,240
My mom was...

151
00:09:45,750 --> 00:09:47,150
was a really good person.

152
00:09:47,630 --> 00:09:48,670
That's for sure.

153
00:09:50,750 --> 00:09:51,550
What else?

154
00:09:53,670 --> 00:09:54,720
Well...

155
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:57,870
When she was young,

156
00:09:57,870 --> 00:09:59,730
she worked at a beverage factory.

157
00:10:03,790 --> 00:10:05,360
A-And then...

158
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:08,480
she seemed to have taught herself...

159
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:10,880
taught herself accounting a few years ago.

160
00:10:13,390 --> 00:10:14,200
Go on.

161
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:16,510
And then she...

162
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:28,250
Now that you're going back,

163
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:30,160
are you still planning to leave?

164
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:36,480
You...

165
00:10:37,030 --> 00:10:37,890
I-I-If...

166
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:39,350
If you haven't made up your mind,

167
00:10:39,350 --> 00:10:39,960
get off the train and think about it.

168
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:40,670
No.

169
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:42,000
I have to see if I can

170
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,930
make it through this winter first.

171
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:04,630
Jia Xin!

172
00:11:06,480 --> 00:11:07,240
Jia Xin!

173
00:11:17,910 --> 00:11:19,030
What are you doing here?

174
00:11:19,030 --> 00:11:19,840
Missed me?

175
00:11:26,270 --> 00:11:27,390
Aren't you short of money?

176
00:11:27,390 --> 00:11:28,080
Here.

177
00:11:31,390 --> 00:11:32,150
Where did you get it?

178
00:11:32,150 --> 00:11:33,670
Don't worry about that.

179
00:11:34,030 --> 00:11:35,360
Remember to pay me back.

180
00:11:36,790 --> 00:11:37,850
Here's your money.

181
00:11:38,790 --> 00:11:40,390
I've already borrowed some.

182
00:11:41,270 --> 00:11:42,030
Really?

183
00:11:42,030 --> 00:11:43,200
Who did you borrow it from?

184
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:43,960
Gong Xue.

185
00:11:44,150 --> 00:11:45,410
She lent me 2,000 yuan.

186
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:48,200
Gong Xue?

187
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:50,410
How do you two know each other?

188
00:11:50,440 --> 00:11:51,840
Did you lose your memory?

189
00:11:52,150 --> 00:11:52,960
Didn't you introduce us

190
00:11:52,960 --> 00:11:54,620
when I came to your workplace?

191
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:56,960
Wait.

192
00:11:57,510 --> 00:11:58,720
You two didn't even speak that day.

193
00:11:58,720 --> 00:11:59,720
How did you get close enough

194
00:11:59,720 --> 00:12:00,510
for her to lend you money?

195
00:12:00,510 --> 00:12:00,910
Well,

196
00:12:01,030 --> 00:12:02,320
we were talking by the entrance that day,

197
00:12:02,320 --> 00:12:03,360
and she overheard us.

198
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:04,820
Then she lent me the money.

199
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:07,670
Take my 2,000

200
00:12:07,670 --> 00:12:09,080
and pay her back.

201
00:12:09,360 --> 00:12:09,720
Pay her back.

202
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:10,910
W-What?

203
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:11,840
No.

204
00:12:13,550 --> 00:12:15,750
Ever heard of
"borrow nine, repay thirteen"?

205
00:12:15,750 --> 00:12:17,210
I borrowed 2,000 from her,

206
00:12:17,440 --> 00:12:19,960
and I have to pay her back

207
00:12:20,150 --> 00:12:21,080
2,888.88 yuan.

208
00:12:21,390 --> 00:12:22,390
Not a cent less.

209
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:35,730
[Gong's Blind Massage]

210
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:40,310
Zhengguang,

211
00:12:40,340 --> 00:12:42,580
a-aren't you off today?

212
00:12:51,150 --> 00:12:51,960
Gong Xue.

213
00:12:51,920 --> 00:12:55,020
[Healing Hands]

214
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:54,240
Why did you lend money to Jia Xin?

215
00:12:55,020 --> 00:12:56,420
[Traditional Chinese Health Therapy;
Dispel Dampness, Boost Qi]

216
00:12:55,390 --> 00:12:56,480
Shouldn't I have?

217
00:12:56,540 --> 00:12:59,000
[Blind Massage;
Relieve Tension & Improve Circulation]

218
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:58,120
Lending is fine,

219
00:12:58,120 --> 00:12:59,960
but you can't charge him
loan-shark interest.

220
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:02,960
What's all this
"borrow nine, repay thirteen" stuff?

221
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:04,870
I need to make money too.

222
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:06,270
Besides,

223
00:13:06,360 --> 00:13:07,960
we already agreed on the terms.

224
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:09,290
Why are you sticking your nose into this?

225
00:13:09,290 --> 00:13:18,560
[Therapeutic Massage;
Daily Care, Pain Relief]

226
00:13:11,550 --> 00:13:13,000
You two met through me,

227
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:13,670
right?

228
00:13:14,670 --> 00:13:15,480
So what?

229
00:13:16,030 --> 00:13:17,270
Don't come to me if something goes wrong.

230
00:13:17,270 --> 00:13:18,480
It's fine.

231
00:13:18,630 --> 00:13:19,910
I've already lent him the money.

232
00:13:19,910 --> 00:13:21,910
Worst case, he goes back on his word.

233
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:25,000
But I believe he won't.

234
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:26,840
Why do you believe

235
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:27,390
he won't?

236
00:13:28,320 --> 00:13:30,390
Because he has a nice voice.

237
00:13:31,390 --> 00:13:32,910
Voices don't lie.

238
00:13:48,670 --> 00:13:50,530
What are you really trying to ask?

239
00:13:54,030 --> 00:13:54,840
I...

240
00:14:01,630 --> 00:14:03,560
Your heart is beating really fast.

241
00:14:04,080 --> 00:14:05,340
You seem very nervous.

242
00:14:07,630 --> 00:14:08,480
I'm not.

243
00:14:09,530 --> 00:14:13,010
[Therapeutic Massage;
Daily Care, Pain Relief]

244
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:15,140
What are you doing?

245
00:14:16,890 --> 00:14:20,220
[Traditional Chinese Health Therapy;
Dispel Dampness, Boost Qi]

246
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:20,040
Which one of you is massaging me anyway?

247
00:14:20,600 --> 00:14:21,360
Mr. Wu?

248
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:24,130
You know each other?

249
00:14:24,550 --> 00:14:26,030
Perfect. Then this client's yours.

250
00:14:26,030 --> 00:14:26,870
Get to work.

251
00:14:27,870 --> 00:14:28,670
Wait...

252
00:14:33,870 --> 00:14:35,080
You like Xue?

253
00:14:37,790 --> 00:14:39,270
No, don't talk nonsense.

254
00:14:40,030 --> 00:14:40,840
That's good.

255
00:14:41,030 --> 00:14:42,960
I don't think she likes you anyway.

256
00:14:43,320 --> 00:14:44,650
Are you any good at this?

257
00:14:46,240 --> 00:14:48,040
Don't go pressing random spots.

258
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:52,120
Zhengguang,

259
00:14:52,750 --> 00:14:54,480
you were really rough with that massage.

260
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:55,150
Why do I get the feeling

261
00:14:55,150 --> 00:14:56,720
you're using this chance
to get back at me?

262
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:57,480
No.

263
00:14:58,630 --> 00:14:59,270
Alright.

264
00:14:59,510 --> 00:15:00,510
Take care, Mr. Wu.

265
00:15:07,440 --> 00:15:08,240
Zhengguang.

266
00:15:09,630 --> 00:15:11,600
I know Gong Yi and his daughter

267
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:12,240
quite well.

268
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:14,370
We've known each other for a long time.

269
00:15:14,910 --> 00:15:15,720
Their family's eyes

270
00:15:15,720 --> 00:15:17,920
really do light up at the sight of money.

271
00:15:18,670 --> 00:15:21,200
-Mr. Wu, I think sometimes you...
-Calm down.

272
00:15:21,910 --> 00:15:24,110
Doesn't medical treatment cost money?

273
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:26,550
When I say that,

274
00:15:28,720 --> 00:15:30,480
I mean it literally.

275
00:15:46,630 --> 00:15:47,300
[Exit] [Entrance] [Tickets]

276
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,250
Where are you going?

277
00:15:51,390 --> 00:15:53,390
I'm going back to my parents' place.

278
00:15:53,550 --> 00:15:54,410
What about you?

279
00:15:54,670 --> 00:15:55,530
I'm going home.

280
00:15:56,270 --> 00:15:57,730
How are you getting there?

281
00:15:57,790 --> 00:15:58,720
I'll take a taxi.

282
00:15:59,150 --> 00:15:59,840
And you?

283
00:16:01,030 --> 00:16:03,030
I suddenly feel like taking the bus.

284
00:16:03,870 --> 00:16:05,240
Well, I'm off that way, then.

285
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:05,960
Bye-bye.

286
00:16:08,580 --> 00:16:11,330
[Bus]

287
00:16:22,550 --> 00:16:23,990
Why are you back?

288
00:16:24,010 --> 00:16:25,810
Weren't you going to take a taxi?

289
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:31,680
I suddenly feel like taking the bus too.

290
00:16:33,720 --> 00:16:34,520
Let's go then.

291
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:56,570
What are you staring at?

292
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:59,120
Nothing.

293
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:02,550
I was just thinking...

294
00:17:04,589 --> 00:17:06,990
This doesn't seem like something you'd do.

295
00:17:07,640 --> 00:17:10,240
How come you're willing to
take the bus with me?

296
00:17:13,109 --> 00:17:14,770
My rational side tells me that

297
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,400
since I've made up my mind

298
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:17,349
to come back,

299
00:17:17,589 --> 00:17:19,720
I have to... have to make some changes.

300
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:21,680
Like what?

301
00:17:23,589 --> 00:17:24,400
Like...

302
00:17:26,030 --> 00:17:26,960
working hard,

303
00:17:27,240 --> 00:17:28,040
saving money,

304
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:29,640
and improving my relationships

305
00:17:29,640 --> 00:17:31,100
with the people around me.

306
00:17:31,880 --> 00:17:32,680
And, well...

307
00:17:32,790 --> 00:17:35,270
B-Being a bit nicer to Liu Zhengguang.

308
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:39,510
That's it?

309
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:44,360
Nothing else like...

310
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:47,000
Like your relationship with me?

311
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:50,070
Well,

312
00:17:50,070 --> 00:17:51,330
didn't I just say that?

313
00:17:51,640 --> 00:17:53,030
I'll be nicer

314
00:17:53,030 --> 00:17:54,680
to everyone around me.

315
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:56,160
Not just you.

316
00:17:58,110 --> 00:18:00,510
I-I don't see what this has to do with me.

317
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:03,530
It does. Aren't you...

318
00:18:03,590 --> 00:18:04,880
Aren't you one of the people around me?

319
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:05,920
You're included.

320
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:08,070
I'm just not singling you out.

321
00:18:15,590 --> 00:18:16,350
Actually, from...

322
00:18:16,350 --> 00:18:17,880
from the bottom of my heart,

323
00:18:18,270 --> 00:18:19,880
I'm grateful to you for...

324
00:18:20,270 --> 00:18:21,440
for what you...

325
00:18:21,440 --> 00:18:22,240
Shut up.

326
00:18:40,070 --> 00:18:40,720
Thank you.

327
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:47,780
[1314 Funeral Services]

328
00:18:46,070 --> 00:18:47,310
Why are you trying to

329
00:18:47,310 --> 00:18:48,110
build that?

330
00:18:49,350 --> 00:18:51,070
We don't need more shelves.

331
00:18:51,680 --> 00:18:53,310
It's not for goods.

332
00:18:58,550 --> 00:18:59,510
Then what is it for?

333
00:18:59,510 --> 00:19:00,270
I want to

334
00:19:00,290 --> 00:19:02,090
take all those things you stole—

335
00:19:02,350 --> 00:19:04,720
your little trophies—

336
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:07,240
and put them all on this shelf.

337
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:08,690
Didn't you tell me to

338
00:19:08,710 --> 00:19:09,680
throw all those things away?

339
00:19:09,680 --> 00:19:10,790
I was thinking,

340
00:19:11,510 --> 00:19:12,590
if we put them here,

341
00:19:12,790 --> 00:19:15,050
you could look at them whenever you want.

342
00:19:15,110 --> 00:19:17,240
And every time you look at them,

343
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:18,000
you'd feel

344
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:19,400
a sense of satisfaction.

345
00:19:20,270 --> 00:19:21,240
Then maybe you wouldn't feel the urge

346
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:22,480
to steal anymore.

347
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:25,880
Well, you've got that wrong.

348
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:31,160
A shelf this pretty will make me

349
00:19:33,030 --> 00:19:34,270
want to steal

350
00:19:34,270 --> 00:19:35,310
even more.

351
00:19:40,310 --> 00:19:41,110
Amy.

352
00:19:42,880 --> 00:19:43,750
I...

353
00:19:45,400 --> 00:19:47,600
don't want to be apart from you anymore.

354
00:19:49,270 --> 00:19:50,270
Not even for a day.

355
00:19:52,750 --> 00:19:54,720
San...

356
00:19:55,510 --> 00:19:58,480
Then I'll just be more careful
when I steal.

357
00:19:59,110 --> 00:20:00,240
I'm back!

358
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:02,020
What are you doing?

359
00:20:04,350 --> 00:20:05,680
Being all lovey-dovey out in the open

360
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:07,410
without even trying to hide it?

361
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:09,550
Y-You're back.

362
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:12,140
Nothing happened, right?

363
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:13,200
Look.

364
00:20:13,510 --> 00:20:14,910
I got back safe and sound.

365
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:16,110
What are you looking at?

366
00:20:16,110 --> 00:20:17,680
You look so happy.

367
00:20:18,240 --> 00:20:19,480
You must have brought

368
00:20:19,480 --> 00:20:20,940
that "Potato Chips" back.

369
00:20:21,070 --> 00:20:21,790
Where is he?

370
00:20:23,680 --> 00:20:24,350
No.

371
00:20:24,550 --> 00:20:25,880
I didn't bring him back.

372
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:27,330
He didn't come back?

373
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:28,510
No.

374
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:30,510
Then did he come back or not?

375
00:20:30,920 --> 00:20:32,400
H-He's back.

376
00:20:32,510 --> 00:20:33,310
Where is he?

377
00:20:34,680 --> 00:20:36,080
He went back to his house.

378
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:42,000
He came back with you.

379
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:44,600
So have the two of you made any progress?

380
00:20:45,830 --> 00:20:46,440
Yes.

381
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:48,110
But... But not much.

382
00:20:48,350 --> 00:20:49,750
"Not much"?

383
00:20:50,270 --> 00:20:51,050
You traveled

384
00:20:51,080 --> 00:20:53,480
thousands of miles
all by yourself for him.

385
00:20:54,030 --> 00:20:55,400
You didn't beat him up, did you?

386
00:20:55,400 --> 00:20:56,590
You... You...

387
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:58,250
What are you talking about?

388
00:20:58,640 --> 00:21:00,100
You two don't understand.

389
00:21:00,270 --> 00:21:01,640
I'm so gentle.

390
00:21:03,110 --> 00:21:04,400
I'm gonna go change.

391
00:21:05,550 --> 00:21:07,110
Why are you looking at me?

392
00:21:07,510 --> 00:21:09,570
I'm looking to see if you understand.

393
00:21:15,510 --> 00:21:17,310
Zhengguang, I'm back.

394
00:21:20,510 --> 00:21:21,310
Brother.

395
00:21:21,590 --> 00:21:23,640
Although we've only been apart
for a few days,

396
00:21:23,640 --> 00:21:25,500
I've missed you so much, Brother.

397
00:21:31,070 --> 00:21:31,880
Who are you?

398
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:33,680
I'm your brother, Liu Zhengliang.

399
00:21:33,680 --> 00:21:34,680
Who else could I be?

400
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:35,590
No way.

401
00:21:35,750 --> 00:21:36,830
Liu Zhengliang would never

402
00:21:36,830 --> 00:21:37,720
say something like that.

403
00:21:37,720 --> 00:21:38,790
I'm calling the police.

404
00:21:38,790 --> 00:21:39,960
Are you serious?

405
00:21:40,590 --> 00:21:41,850
You're overreacting.

406
00:21:43,160 --> 00:21:43,960
Move aside.

407
00:21:48,350 --> 00:21:49,680
Didn't you go to Fuzhou?

408
00:21:49,680 --> 00:21:50,750
Why are you back?

409
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:53,550
Some things came up.

410
00:21:53,830 --> 00:21:55,070
It's a long story.

411
00:21:56,350 --> 00:21:57,440
You can't just do this.

412
00:21:57,440 --> 00:21:59,240
Didn't I tell you to
let me know in advance?

413
00:21:59,240 --> 00:22:00,240
You gave me no time to

414
00:22:00,240 --> 00:22:00,680
mentally prepare for this.

415
00:22:00,680 --> 00:22:02,210
What are you talking about?

416
00:22:02,550 --> 00:22:03,550
I'm just coming home.

417
00:22:03,550 --> 00:22:05,550
What kind of mental preparation...

418
00:22:09,640 --> 00:22:10,310
Yes.

419
00:22:10,920 --> 00:22:12,250
You're right, Brother.

420
00:22:12,550 --> 00:22:13,750
It's all my fault.

421
00:22:14,070 --> 00:22:14,870
Tell you what.

422
00:22:15,070 --> 00:22:16,590
Next time I come back,

423
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:18,040
I'll tell you in advance.

424
00:22:22,920 --> 00:22:24,590
Then how long are you staying?

425
00:22:26,480 --> 00:22:27,940
Anywhere from a few months

426
00:22:28,160 --> 00:22:29,440
to the rest of my life.

427
00:22:32,070 --> 00:22:33,310
Do you really mean it?

428
00:22:39,310 --> 00:22:40,110
Zhengguang,

429
00:22:40,960 --> 00:22:41,920
you're the only family

430
00:22:41,920 --> 00:22:43,050
I have in this world.

431
00:22:43,790 --> 00:22:45,190
We have to stay together.

432
00:22:50,310 --> 00:22:51,480
Why does it sound so gross

433
00:22:51,480 --> 00:22:52,550
coming out of your mouth?

434
00:22:52,550 --> 00:22:53,480
From now on,

435
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:54,920
I'll fulfill my duty

436
00:22:54,920 --> 00:22:56,120
as your older brother

437
00:22:56,590 --> 00:22:57,990
and take good care of you.

438
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:06,800
What's wrong?

439
00:23:07,550 --> 00:23:08,510
What happened?

440
00:23:09,310 --> 00:23:10,710
What could've happened?

441
00:23:11,880 --> 00:23:12,680
Well?

442
00:23:12,960 --> 00:23:14,110
Are you moved by how much

443
00:23:14,110 --> 00:23:15,000
I've changed?

444
00:23:15,720 --> 00:23:16,440
I...

445
00:23:16,440 --> 00:23:17,880
I don't dare to move.

446
00:23:18,350 --> 00:23:19,160
I feel like you're

447
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:20,200
a monster in disguise.

448
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:21,480
If I make a move, you'll eat me.

449
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:23,210
You're being way too dramatic.

450
00:23:24,960 --> 00:23:25,920
I-I'm a little overwhelmed.

451
00:23:25,920 --> 00:23:27,200
My brain can't...

452
00:23:27,440 --> 00:23:29,440
It's all too much.
I need some time to process this.

453
00:23:29,440 --> 00:23:30,400
I'm off to work.

454
00:23:31,400 --> 00:23:32,200
Brother.

455
00:23:32,830 --> 00:23:33,960
You found a new job?

456
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:35,900
Congratulations. Come here.

457
00:23:40,550 --> 00:23:41,270
Don't move.

458
00:23:42,790 --> 00:23:43,720
Don't come over.

459
00:23:45,200 --> 00:23:46,200
I'm going to work.

460
00:23:49,400 --> 00:23:50,550
Seriously?

461
00:23:52,480 --> 00:23:53,270
Take it easy.

462
00:23:53,590 --> 00:23:55,590
Zhengguang, be careful on the road!

463
00:24:10,400 --> 00:24:11,730
I'm being a bit too much.

464
00:24:22,270 --> 00:24:23,200
All these years,

465
00:24:23,550 --> 00:24:25,030
I seem to have been thinking

466
00:24:25,030 --> 00:24:26,480
only about how to get away from here—

467
00:24:26,480 --> 00:24:27,440
the further

468
00:24:27,550 --> 00:24:28,640
the better.

469
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:30,160
But when I really found myself

470
00:24:30,160 --> 00:24:32,220
with absolutely nothing, I realized

471
00:24:32,720 --> 00:24:34,310
how good it feels to be home.

472
00:24:35,160 --> 00:24:36,960
Being with family

473
00:24:37,960 --> 00:24:38,760
feels so good.

474
